    generated by exactly the dozen the coins already work. -/
theorem hextorus_generators_are_the_jobs : 2 * 6 = 12 := by decide

/-- THE GENUS LADDER PRICES IN COINS: the deficit 2g − 2 over g = 1..6 walks the evens [0, 2, 4, 6, 8, 10] — the
    torus contains at 0 (containment_is_genus_one), the double torus mints the 2, and every further handle adds
    one coin-pair until the hextorus owes the ten. A ladder of shapes, one price list, all even — the coins' own
    multiples. -/
theorem genus_ladder_prices_in_coins : List.map (fun g => 2 * g - 2) [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6] = [0, 2, 4, 6, 8, 10] := by decide

/-- THE 7-TORUS IS THE 7-QUBIT FOLD, IN ITS OWN NUMBERS: Pascal's row 7 — [1, 7, 21, 35, 35, 21, 7, 1] — sums to
    128 = 2⁷, the uuid's bit count and the RULE every file header states (one uuid = 128 bits folded across 7
